# Whole V3 frontier with the frozen single-owner wave: read-only compatibility audit

**Decision boundary.** The four-file V3 variant is structurally composable with frozen product `dec7509b3a18b2d71e27de023419f45c32fb10e7`, but it is not an admitted product wave or a demonstrated parity fix. Preserve the entire `01f2395..aac036f` V3 change (the archived `v3-original.patch` hashes to `02e2d697cf08f95abee99170abc47b71012f5653ba31ab21e7a7bcfffa7ca2b6`) for any combination experiment. Do not transplant only the full-range helper: admission, iterator mode, rollback/fallback, counters, and cold-output tests form one proof.

## Composition and work removed

The only production-code overlap is `state.rs` and test-only `work_attribution.rs`. The current wave changes single-owner preflight/routing, full-text replacement seeding, and publication acknowledgement in `state.rs`; V3 adds `planner_full_frontier_source_range` and dispatch in `append_planner_gather`. These edit different hunks. V3 also changes `codec_gather.rs` and test-only `transport/bitmap_replay_auth.rs`; the current wave changes neither. The current TypeScript direct arena writer has no V3 overlap or ABI dependency. A combined implementation needs an intentional merge of the two counter structs/initializers and test expectations, not a silent overwrite. The current commit's `publication_ack_only_visits` and `preflight_seeded_old_units` must survive beside V3's three gather counters.

Current `prepare_retained_order(Gather)` makes `order_sort_scratch` from pending plus unpublished preparation IDs, sorts by renderer order, rejects lifecycle changes, missing/changed source counts, decorations, pending removals, and stale order identities. V3 then admits its single `0..end` rope range only when that scratch covers **every** active owner in exact order, old gather ranges are contiguous in both source and record coordinates, each old/new source count agrees, both active and committed decorations are absent, each owner's retained unpublished intervals are empty for zero sources or one full interval, and the final source end equals `gathered_source_count`. Missing/invalid state falls back to the existing owner-range iterator; non-sparse/replacement and fresh paths remain unchanged. The `None` interval case is accepted by V3 as a full recomposition case; it is not proof that every semantic mask bit is dirty. Inspect the producer's mask contract when combining.

On admission, `RetainedRanges` supplies one rope range instead of asking `OwnerRanges::next()` for each owner/interval. The callback still advances through `planner_gather_owners`, resolves each owner/range and font binding, checks source-count mismatch, updates selected source rows and record cursors, and may stop into the existing whole-gather replacement path. The immutable prior rope root remains cloned for callback prefix/gap summaries until the transactional append returns; `self.sources` is restored on error. This removes owner-range iteration and repeated rope range dispatch only. It does **not** remove source traversal, eager per-setter semantic/render preparation, per-owner callback work, field reads/writes, Codec execution, plan compilation, or renderer publication. The V3 admission pass itself inspects every active owner and adds branch/maintenance cost; a small dense improvement cannot be assumed to pay for that pass.

The frozen wave's acknowledgement changes when an already committed, unpublished owner is marked published and zeroes its semantic masks. It does not clear the unpublished frontier before gather: `commit_paragraphs(true)` runs at publication commit after preparation. Pending IDs take precedence over unpublished IDs, and the current wave explicitly commits newer pending work before an older acknowledgement. V3's admission therefore sees the pending/unpublished union and the pre-publication intervals/masks. If the combined code changes this order, it could admit a clean or stale owner across a full range; keep the ordering invariant explicit. An accepted independent split remains a separate copy lifetime; V3 must not borrow it or cause it to observe later edits.

## Required discriminating proof if the complete variant is tried

Retain the V3 dense 1,024-owner cold gather and physical draw/buffer/placement comparison, full-range versus owner-range counter assertions, scattered/partial interval fallback, callback failure/source-root restoration, and count-change suffix stop tests. Run them against the *combined* source, together with the frozen wave's same-length replacement/roundtrip, pending plus unpublished overlap, rejection/retry, ABI-byte and arena-offset tests. Specifically prove a prior full replacement that is read through measure/glyphs/split, then overwritten before publication, still produces cold-equivalent bytes/order and leaves the first split independent. Authenticate the combined native/Wasm product before any matched matrix. None of these checks was run in this read-only audit.

## Cost judgment

The frozen wave already removes an old UTF-16 seed copy, repeated single-owner routing, empty wire-section work, and no-op stage commits. V3 attacks a different, narrower publication-gather iterator cost, so there is no direct duplicated deletion. It also adds an O(owners) admission scan and a second range mode with rollback/fallback obligations. That complexity is justified only if a combined, authenticated fixed-20 candidate closes meaningful **complete-operation** dense losses while preserving the other required families and exact output. The currently supplied fixed-20 candidate rows are 512: 8.294/8.837/9.001 ms and 1,024: 17.485/18.344/18.585 ms (p50/p90/p95); they have no newly matched control and therefore establish no parity decision. Historical profile outliers and a 5% floor cannot supply a latency claim. If matched controls reach parity with the frozen wave, stop and leave V3 preserved. If losses remain, a bounded whole-V3 combination is reasonable to test, but this source audit cannot predict that it will close them.

Sources: frozen-wave report `benches/reports/held-single-owner-local-2026-10-22/README.md`; exact product diff `01f2395..dec7509b`; four-file V3 diff `01f2395..aac036f`; current producers/consumers in `state.rs`, `codec_gather.rs`, `positioning.rs`, and `frame-wire.ts`. No code, runtime, harness, lock, tests, builds, benchmarks, or checkout were changed by this audit.
